(4565090, 656579, 90495, '<td valign="top">I hate trainers. But I like this photo. Nice colours.</td>', 'I hate trainers. But I like this photo. Nice colours.', '2008-03-15 11:04:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(4565100, 654980, 66597, '<td valign="top">I''m having trouble getting the connection between being nude with high heels and doing math. If the lines of her body formed a triangle, then I could see it, but they don''t. Also, the triangle on the board appears to be an isosceles triangle, which indeed can be solved via Pythagorian''s theorem, but not the one you have on the board - that''s for a right triangle. The theorem for an isosceles triangle is: h=sqrt(b^2-1/4a^2). It has the unfortunate effect for me of the woman appearing as a sex object (nude), but not intelligent enough to understand her basic math. I realize this may not be intentional, but I would like to know what the thought process was behind this photo.</td>', 'I''m having trouble getting the connection between being nude with high heels and doing math. If the lines of her body formed a triangle, then I could see it, but they don''t. Also, the triangle on the board appears to be an isosceles triangle, which indeed can be solved via Pythagorian''s theorem, but not the one you have on the board - that''s for a right triangle. The theorem for an isosceles triangle is: h=sqrt(b^2-1/4a^2). It has the unfortunate effect for me of the woman appearing as a sex object (nude), but not intelligent enough to understand her basic math. I realize this may not be intentional, but I would like to know what the thought process was behind this photo.', '2008-03-15 11:13:47.000000', NULL, 1),
